e discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\n- There are removable discontinuities at both $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307120 1113 #uuid "3f6ba6a9-669c-53ec-9eb7-450cfe9629e8" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307120 1145 "The function is continuous at $x=-1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nOn the other hand, the function has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(1)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)\\ne f(1)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=1$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, II is true while I and III are false." 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307122 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307123 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307124 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307125 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307126 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1041 "selection" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307126 13194139534744 true] [17592186307121 1110 #uuid "da18e595-bfb7-5db8-b733-c988c6b371bd" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307122 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307122 1111 #uuid "e299d61e-d811-575f-8652-9c2781d8496e" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307123 1034 "I only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307123 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307123 1111 #uuid "4e308afc-b327-5302-9136-42a1190555f1" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307124 1034 "III only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307124 1103 #edb/ref 17