se." 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307129 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307130 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307131 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307132 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307133 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1041 "selection" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307129 13194139534744 true] [17592186307128 1110 #uuid "b083d42b-d207-593c-9314-275453cff8f4" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307129 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307129 1111 #uuid "3634d29f-864c-5612-a3a0-2d1adfd25709" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307130 1034 "I only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307130 1111 #uuid "75e55be7-ecaf-5ce3-9ace-15055cf1d531" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307131 1034 "III only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307131 1111 #uuid "12828aa8-0496-5f7b-b71e-512ec654adf7" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307132 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307132 1111 #uuid "6c868039-c6bf-5e41-a903-d151527d60bd" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307133 1034 "II only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307133 1111 #uuid "ca8fba5c-4423-5a82-823f-7e602b0e9309" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307134 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307135 13194139534744 true] [17592186307134 1089 "q-48111" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307134 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534744 true] [17592186307134 1100 "Which of the following functions has a removable discontinuity at $x=2?$" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307134 1113 #uuid "c8a1f245-c03d-5454-853a-837712e2f33c" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307134 1145 "The function $p(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $p(2)=2$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}p(x)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}p(x)\\ne p(2)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=2$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/fbc65d4168ce2f6747e75a606b3ccc175f9a68d98f718e473255f085d929c334.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that the functions $h(x)$ and $q(x)$ are continuous at $x=2,$ while $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ both have a discontinuity at $x=2$ but they are *not* removable." 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307136 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307137 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307138 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307139 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307140 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1041 "selection" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307138 13194139534744 true] [17592186307135 1110 #uuid "99f5a4c9-0afd-5eec-a774-22b631ae61ad" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307136 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/937d91014870e27a93c247e87b7008f5c63807df764503fc7a9ebccfa8044d65.png" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307136 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534744 true] [17592186307136 1111 #uuid "9a35281b-4721-56cd-8095-dbe034073f27" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307137 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/5c22017c6a89ddb6a4ff481de6b210e272075ca2e7d492785d4be4950982cce0.png" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534744 true] [17592186307137 1111 #uuid "2cba0e29-d85c-5b4f-922d-2c8134e3bdff" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307138 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/fbc65d4168ce2f6747e75a606b3ccc175f9a68d98f718e473255f085d929c334.png" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534744 true] [17592186307138 1111 #uuid "8d59779b-2d58-5f31-be35-d65255227a64" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307139 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/ebef782bf2d2df29c0b016e5f2e3ae42eab200f3ae502d1eea7fe522ff0f1b5a.png" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534744 true] [17592186307139 1111 #uuid "8b30df25-76d2-59d7-af44-cd8741448dd9" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307140 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/bbe9ecff2a793d2cadb42c6dedfab841869fae3215f6da0d8b6da7b9fbfa4ec1.png" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534744 true] [17592186307140 1111 #uuid "f0b2748c-4292-5956-a2d4-979418b9dbdf" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307141 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307142 13194139534744 true] [17592186307141 1089 "q-48125" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307141 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534744 true] [17592186307141 1100 "Given the functions $\\,f(x),\\,g(x)\\,$ and $\\,h(x)\\,$ below, which of them has a point discontinuity at $x=0?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x}+3 & x<0 \\\\ 4, & x=0 \\\\ 3x+4, & x>0\\end{aligned} \\\\  \\\\ g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}2(x+1), & x<0 \\\\ 0, & x=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2, & x>0\\end{aligned} \\\\  \\\\ h(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+1, & x\\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5}+12x+1, & x>0\\end{aligned}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307141 1113 #uuid "a51cbbd3-b785-5c40-be75-e613ee48e2aa" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307141 1145 "Let's check each function, in turn:\n\nLet's check our continuity conditions for $f(x)$ at $x=0:$\n\n- $f(0)=4$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x) & ={2}^{0}+3=4, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x) & =3(0)+4=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=4.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=f(0)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0.$\n\nNow, let's check our continuity conditions for $g(x)$ at $x=0:$\n\n- $g(0)=0$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}g(x) & =2(0+1)=2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}g(x) & ={0}^{2}+2=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x)=2.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x)\\ne g(0)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $g(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$ It's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=0$ is a point discontinuity. \n\nFinally, let's check our continuity conditions for $h(x)$ at $x=0:$\n\n- $h(0)=2(0)^{2}+1=1$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}h(x) & =2(0)^{2}+1=1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}h(x) & =(0)^{5}+12(0)+1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}h(x)=1.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}h(x)=h(0)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nSo, the function $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $g(x)$ has a point discontinuity at $x=0.$" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307143 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307144 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307145 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307146 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307147 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1041 "selection" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307145 13194139534744 true] [17592186307142 1110 #uuid "e49579b5-6c9a-537b-afe7-9a57de71cbf1" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307143 1034 "$f(x)$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307143 1111 #uuid "984d002d-b3d9-5fff-85b5-920571715f59" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307144 1034 "$g(x)$ and $h(x)$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307144 1111 #uuid "e8c0e10c-0f05-5103-b9fc-adcc899df027" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307145 1034 "$g(x)$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307145 1111 #uuid "a031c657-25d5-51ae-a85c-2e621b1d29e5" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307146 1034 "$h(x)$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307146 1111 #uuid "30cfde9a-83c4-5a38-bea3-ac4bf8d7ca24" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307147 1034 "$f(x)$ and $h(x)$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307147 1111 #uuid "da74d5a3-27c1-5574-aea9-a73dce167a2c" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307148 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307149 13194139534744 true] [17592186307148 1089 "q-48128" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307148 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534744 true] [17592186307148 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/e3fa6d490da81fca9b24f9de41b01daaa957f574375cc8523aec448a0ef73015.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above. For what values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x)$ have a removable discontinuity?" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307148 1113 #uuid "660180ee-565e-5382-abb3-a2ce13e9f578" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307148 1145 "The function has a discontinuity at $x=-2.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-2)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)\\ne f(-2)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=-2$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nNote that the function also has a discontinuity at $x=2.$ but it is not a point discontinuity. Checking the conditions, we find that\n\n- $f(2)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\times $\n\nSo this time, the second condition failed, and therefore $x=2$ is not a point discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $x=-2$ only." 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307150 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307151 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307152 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307153 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307154 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1041 "selection" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307153 13194139534744 true] [17592186307149 1110 #uuid "a95f6f1a-b250-5e5f-a49b-9a562bd57875" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307150 1034 "$x=2$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307150 1111 #uuid "4fba041a-00f4-56c2-b579-8ed9efc55eeb" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307151 1034 "$x=-2$ and $x=2$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307151 1111 #uuid "2500e4a4-aaad-5b59-ab49-e3398e8d6c3c" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307152 1034 "$x=-3$ and $x=-2$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307152 1111 #uuid "ae1dd774-f727-53a8-82a9-f85ec6f386f1" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307153 1034 "$x=-2$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307153 1111 #uuid "1238ed40-c4bf-5e3f-8056-29ddaeb4f20b" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307154 1034 "$x=-3$ and $x=2$ only" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534744 true] [17592186307154 1111 #uuid "87ac35e5-2b80-5f8a-9137-9fd3de35128f" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307155 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307156 13194139534744 true] [17592186307155 1089 "q-48161" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307155 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534744 true] [17592186307155 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/b92c2d0e713799d32f1be12b6cba56231af27ccc7a013e8726ab3b09289e69d8.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above. For what values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x)$ have a point discontinuity?" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307155 1113 #uuid "a85b78fd-d65c-5ded-9498-c7b6781a7e0f" 13194139534744 true] [17592186307155 1145 "The function has a discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(3)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)\\ne f(3)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=3$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nNote that the function also has a discontinuity at $x=-3,$ but it is not a point discontinuity. Checking the conditions, we find that\n\n- $f(-3)$ does not exist. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo this time, the first condition failed, and therefore $x=-3$ is not a point discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $x=3$ only." 13194139534744 true] [17592186307156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307157 13194139534744 true] [17592186307156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307158 13194139534744 true] [17592186307156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307159 13194139534744 true] [17592186307156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307160 13194139534744 true] [17592186307156 10